    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>A hail claim denial is a decision you can question. Start by finding the exact reason and the policy language behind it.</li>
<li>Most denials rest on a few themes: no hail damage found, wear and tear, pre-existing damage, late reporting, an exclusion, or damage below the deductible.</li>
<li>Answer the stated reason with matching evidence: labeled photos, a qualified inspection report, and NOAA storm data for your address and date.</li>
<li>Request a reinspection in writing. If the dispute is about the amount of a covered loss, your policy’s appraisal clause may apply.</li>
<li>TDI complaints are available if the insurer is unresponsive. For lawsuits and deadlines, talk to a Texas attorney.</li>
